<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Olaf Frederick Nelson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1883–1944</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as O. F. Nelson</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Olaf Frederick Nelson was a Samoan merchant of Swedish and Samoan descent and a leader of the Mau, the non-violent movement against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> rule in Western Samoa. The New Zealand administration exiled him twice, in 1928 and 1933. After the police shooting of Mau marchers on Black Saturday in 1929, the movement continued until New Zealand changed course in 1936.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/olaf-frederick-nelson.jpg" alt="Olaf Frederick Nelson" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ta%E2%80%99isi_O.F._Nelson_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
